1128 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Text/Rect[34.865999 739.30538 50.865999 755.30538]/C[1 .98 .82]/Popup 1129 0 R/P 173 0 R/F 28/Contents(SUMMARY: Agentic RL needs isolated stateful environments at scale; 7 workload properties \(bursty 32K-sandbox jobs, sparse CPU, statefulness, heterogeneity, low image reuse, untrusted agents, interruptibility\) each map to a mechanism.\n\n\nCRITIQUE: Excellent taxonomy discipline, but properties come from one company's workload; burst sizes reflect DeepSeek's GRPO batches, generality unproven.)/Name/Comment/AP<</N 1149 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A5)>>
endobj

1129 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1128 0 R/Rect[32 729.89 232 829.89]>>
endobj

1130 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Text/AP<</N 1150 0 R>>/Contents(SUMMARY: libdsec SDK deliberately NOT a semantic abstraction - callers pick among FnCall/container/microVM/fullVM. Scale: 160 nodes, 3M sandboxes/day, 380K concurrent, >5K creations/s per scale unit.\n\n\n\nCRITIQUE: Honest refusal to abstract, but burden shifts to users - no data on wrong-backend costs. Numbers are per-unit; fleet total undisclosed.)/Rect[34.866 116.619388 54.866 136.61939]/C[1 .98 .82]/F 28/DA(//Helvetica 12 Tf 0 g)/Popup 1131 0 R/Name/Comment/Border[0 0 0]>>
endobj

1131 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1130 0 R/Rect[32 729.89 232 829.89]>>
endobj

1132 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Text/Rect[34.865999 628.71438 50.865999 644.71438]/C[1 .98 .82]/Popup 1133 0 R/P 426 0 R/F 28/Contents(SUMMARY: Stateless control plane throughout: apiserver keeps no sandbox state \(ID encodes owning edge\), watcher rebuildable, placement = filter + rank random sample. Node: edge/aether/chronus. IAM: multi-level nesting, agents as first-class principals. Cloud bursting: 30TB EROFS set covers 70% of tasks.\n\n\nCRITIQUE: 'No durable control-plane state' is the core idea, underemphasized. No edge-failure analysis; no placement-quality comparison vs coordinated schedulers.)/Name/Comment/AP<</N 1151 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A3)>>
endobj

1133 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1132 0 R/Rect[32 729.89 232 829.89]>>
endobj

1134 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Text/Rect[34.865999 518.32839 50.865999 534.32839]/C[1 .98 .82]/Popup 1135 0 R/P 679 0 R/F 28/Contents(SUMMARY: One production week: p99 4,044 sandboxes/task; 90% of sandboxes use <=5% requested CPU; median life 17min, p99 >3h; 130TB artifacts, median fanout 3; runtime touches only 4-13% of image bytes.\n\n\nCRITIQUE: Strongest section - real distributions, each tied to a mechanism. But one week, one snapshot, containers+microVMs only.)/Name/Comment/AP<</N 1152 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A2)>>
endobj

1135 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1134 0 R/Rect[32 729.89 232 829.89]>>
endobj

1136 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Text/Rect[34.865999 171.50434 50.865999 187.50434]/C[1 .98 .82]/Popup 1137 0 R/P 738 0 R/F 28/Contents(SUMMARY: \(1\) composable EROFS layers via overlayfs \(O\(m*N\)->O\(m\) rebuilds, 30-LoC dockerd patch\); \(2\) memory: virtio-pmem+DAX \(-40.2% peak\) + DAMON->balloon FPR \(-21.2%\); \(3\) SCHED_IDLE + core scheduling \(45.2%->17.3%\); \(4\) on-demand loading shaped by 3FS asymmetry: writes local, reads bulk, metadata local.\n\n\nCRITIQUE: Virtue = fitting stock kernel features to measured asymmetries. Mechanisms never evaluated jointly \(e.g., DAMON reclaim vs on-demand refetch\).)/Name/Comment/AP<</N 1153 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A2)>>
endobj

1137 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1136 0 R/Rect[32 729.89 232 829.89]>>
endobj

1138 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Text/Rect[34.865999 610.9324 50.865999 626.9324]/C[1 .98 .82]/Popup 1139 0 R/P 536 0 R/F 28/Contents(SUMMARY: pack_diff turns interactive sessions into reusable environments \(agents build envs for agents\); V4.1 moves rollout to sandbox+worker as single source of truth \(no more command-log replay\); pause = freeze+memory.reclaim / snapshot+kill; real exploit catalog incl. XFS_IOC_SWAPEXT extent-swap that corrupted XFS; AppArmor + per-sandbox eBPF allowlists.\n\n\nCRITIQUE: The misbehavior catalog is the paper's most valuable public artifact. Honest scoping \(no defense vs kernel-bug destruction\). Gap: reward-hacking detection is purely reactive.)/Name/Comment/AP<</N 1154 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A5)>>
endobj

1139 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1138 0 R/Rect[32 729.89 232 829.89]>>
endobj

1140 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Text/Rect[34.865999 191.82837 50.865999 207.82837]/C[1 .98 .82]/Popup 1141 0 R/P 553 0 R/F 28/Contents(SUMMARY: power-of-k placement + local in-flight overlays + edge authority; BGP/ECMP VIPs; regular from-scratch IaC cluster resets; zero kernel mods; Rust OverlayBD/ublk open-sourced; GPU FnCall via MIG + warm pools; 3FS: 20x15TB SSD + 2x400Gbps RDMA per server.\n\n\nCRITIQUE: 'Prove IaC rebuilds everything by resetting regularly' deserves imitation. Grab-bag section; placement strategy belongs in section 3.)/Name/Comment/AP<</N 1155 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A7)>>
endobj

1141 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1140 0 R/Rect[32 729.89 232 829.89]>>
endobj

1142 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Text/Rect[34.865999 678.6784 50.865999 694.6784]/C[1 .98 .82]/Popup 1143 0 R/P 578 0 R/F 28/Contents(SUMMARY: 8,192-container burst: on-demand EROFS ~= fully-local \(35 vs 60 min eager, -57% writes\); EROFS vs tar 1.76x faster, -5.5x writes; pmem -40.2% peak mem but +CPU \(26.5->41.4%\); QoS: 45.2%->17.3% latency inflation.\n\n\nCRITIQUE: Right baselines incl. fully-local upper bound; negative results reported. But 10 nodes vs 160-node production, no end-to-end RL throughput, and section 6 co-design excluded from evaluation.)/Name/Comment/AP<</N 1156 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A3)>>
endobj

1143 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1142 0 R/Rect[32 729.89 232 829.89]>>
endobj

1144 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Text/Rect[34.865999 440.56239 50.865999 456.56239]/C[1 .98 .82]/Popup 1145 0 R/P 648 0 R/F 28/Contents(SUMMARY: vs serverless \(stateless/high-fanout\), LLM code-exec platforms \(model-centric\), image formats \(builds on EROFS/DADI\), isolation research \(integrates, not invents\), RL systems \(env as black box\).\n\n\nCRITIQUE: Accurate, modest positioning. Missing: quantified comparison vs Kubernetes - the rejected default is never measured.)/Name/Comment/AP<</N 1157 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A4)>>
endobj

1145 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1144 0 R/Rect[32 729.89 232 829.89]>>
endobj

1146 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Text/Rect[34.865999 563.57937 50.865999 579.57937]/C[1 .98 .82]/Popup 1147 0 R/P 222 0 R/F 28/Contents(SUMMARY: Unified multi-backend sandbox platform; composable layers, memory sharing/reclaim, CPU QoS, 3FS on-demand loading, RL co-design.\n\n\nOVERALL: Classic systems method done well. Lasting contributions: agentic-RL workload characterization, misbehavior catalog, proof that stock Linux suffices at 380K concurrency. Shortfalls: single-workload generality, isolated evaluations, no K8s head-to-head.)/Name/Comment/AP<</N 1158 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A3)>>
endobj

1147 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1146 0 R/Rect[32 729.89 232 829.89]>>
endobj

